From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] nx2: while the pool is short, idle clean textures are freed before anything is refused (waveydude's 0912 part, EDEN_NX2_IDLE_TEXTURE_PRESSURE), off by default

What: the texture cache counts its own images against fixed marks (2,560 / 3,328 MiB). On the
console the pool is shared with the game's memory, the heap and the driver, so the cache can sit far
under its marks while the pool has nothing left. In a hand-played T151 session (13 Nov, 15 min, crash
in a new area) the largest free block was 1-14 MiB from minute 8 to the end while the cache held
1.1-1.8 GiB, and at a refusal "538 images, 608 MiB, unused for 10 frames" were still there
(EDEN_REFUSED_IMAGES). EDEN_NX2_REFUSAL_EVICT frees such images, but only after a refusal, and a
refusal on the console is where things already break (driver pipeline builds, guest writes).

With EDEN_NX2_IDLE_TEXTURE_PRESSURE=1 (exact "1", read once, PS5 only, and only when the wrapper
gives the pool's largest free block): at the end of a frame, at most every 250 ms, when that block
is known and under 1 GiB, RefusalEvict runs as for a 64 MiB refusal (up to 128 images or 128 MiB, at
most 4,096 LRU entries looked at) with two differences: images must be unused for 10 frames and
1 s (not 300 ms), and nothing the GPU wrote goes (GpuModified is passed over, so RefusalDownloadEvict
is never asked for either). What goes is uploaded again from guest memory when it is used again,
as after AreaEvict. The frame clock runs with the switch (as with REFUSAL_EVICT or CLEAN_BY_TIME).
Its passes show in the EDEN_REFUSAL_EVICT lines as "idle pressure" (the first 16, then every 64th)
and count in their totals.

Price: images freed early come back as uploads (and ASTC decodes) if the area uses them again:
hitches at a camera turn. Pairs with EDEN_NX2_REFUSAL_EVICT=1 (not needed).

Changed from his: RefusalEvict's third parameter is `idle` (his idle_pressure); his per-pass
LOG_INFO line is left out (every 250 ms at 0 MiB free would be four lines a second), the existing
EDEN_REFUSAL_EVICT line says "idle pressure" instead; the switch helper sits in frame_clock.h next
to RefusalEvictEnabled.

Off: one static bool more in the frame-clock test and one at the frame's end; RefusalEvict's
callers pass false (one more test per looked-at image, only when a refusal pass runs); a time
point in TextureCache. Not in the kept-store stamp.

Origin and credit: waveydude, ocarina-private patch 0912 ("T120: integrate Build O and add idle
texture pressure cleanup"), commits dc8796d and 3db885a.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/frame_clock.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/frame_clock.h
index 3f2594b..52e4305 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/frame_clock.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/frame_clock.h
@@ -35,6 +35,14 @@ namespace VideoCommon {
     return enabled;
 }
 
+/// EDEN_NX2_IDLE_TEXTURE_PRESSURE=1 (exact "1", PS5 only; waveydude's 0912): every 250 ms at a
+/// frame's end, while the pool's largest free block is known and under 1 GiB, RefusalEvict frees
+/// clean images unused for 10 frames and 1 s without waiting for a refusal (TextureCache::TickFrame).
+[[nodiscard]] inline bool IdleTexturePressureEnabled() noexcept {
+    static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_NX2_IDLE_TEXTURE_PRESSURE");
+    return enabled;
+}
+
 /// A frame count read as time at the reference rate of 60 frames a second.
 [[nodiscard]] constexpr std::chrono::microseconds FramesAsTime(u64 frames) noexcept {
     return std::chrono::microseconds{static_cast<s64>((std::min)(frames, u64{1} << 40) * 1'000'000 / 60)};
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index 7f9cc25..67ed95c 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -1607,9 +1607,10 @@ std::optional<u64> TextureCache<P>::OldCutoff(u64 frames, u64 floor) const {
 // images already go again when one was deleted (has_deleted_images), as for JoinImages' own deletes.
 // Lines in stderr: EDEN_REFUSAL_EVICT, the first 16 and then every 64th.
 template <class P>
-u64 TextureCache<P>::RefusalEvict(u64 wanted, bool in_join) {
+u64 TextureCache<P>::RefusalEvict(u64 wanted, bool in_join, bool idle) {
     constexpr u64 MinFrames = 10;
-    constexpr auto MinAge = std::chrono::milliseconds(300);
+    // EDEN_NX2_IDLE_TEXTURE_PRESSURE (idle): nothing was refused yet, so a longer age.
+    const auto MinAge = std::chrono::milliseconds(idle ? 1000 : 300);
     constexpr size_t MaxImages = 128;
     constexpr size_t MaxVisits = 4096;
     if (frame_tick <= MinFrames) {
@@ -1643,7 +1644,8 @@ u64 TextureCache<P>::RefusalEvict(u64 wanted, bool in_join) {
         if (True(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::IsDecoding) ||
             (KeepAsyncDecodedFrames() != 0 &&
              True(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::AsynchronousDecode)) ||
-            KeptRemade(image) || joining(image_id)) {
+            KeptRemade(image) || joining(image_id) ||
+            (idle && True(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::GpuModified))) {
             return false;
         }
         if (IsDownloadable(image) && False(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::BadOverlap)) {
@@ -1696,7 +1698,8 @@ u64 TextureCache<P>::RefusalEvict(u64 wanted, bool in_join) {
                      "EDEN_REFUSAL_EVICT %s at frame %llu for %llu MiB: %zu images, %llu MiB "
                      "deleted, %zu GPU-written left for the frame's end, %zu looked at; %llu "
                      "passes, %llu images, %llu MiB so far, %llu retries, %llu fitted\n",
-                     in_join ? "image" : "frame end", static_cast<unsigned long long>(frame_tick),
+                     in_join ? "image" : idle ? "idle pressure" : "frame end",
+                     static_cast<unsigned long long>(frame_tick),
                      static_cast<unsigned long long>(wanted >> 20), doomed.size(),
                      static_cast<unsigned long long>(bytes >> 20), dirty, (std::min)(visits, MaxVisits),
                      static_cast<unsigned long long>(refusal_evict_passes),
@@ -1826,7 +1829,7 @@ void TextureCache<P>::TickFrame() {
     if (pe_busy) Eden::AstcPolicy::Frame();
     // EDEN_UP_HITCH_TRACE: the frame that just ended, when it was long.
     HitchTrace::EndFrame(frame_tick);
-    if (CleanByTime() || RefusalEvictEnabled()) {
+    if (CleanByTime() || RefusalEvictEnabled() || IdleTexturePressureEnabled()) {
         frame_clock.EndFrame(frame_tick, std::chrono::steady_clock::now());
     }
     // Upload buffers grown for one huge image (title 1's 341 MiB terrain layer pools) are freed
@@ -2167,6 +2170,21 @@ void TextureCache<P>::TickFrame() {
         }
         refusal_evicts_this_frame = 0;
     }
+#ifdef PS5_NATIVE
+    // EDEN_NX2_IDLE_TEXTURE_PRESSURE=1 (waveydude's 0912): the pool is short but nothing has been
+    // refused yet: clean images unused for 1 s go now, up to 128 MiB a pass, a pass every 250 ms.
+    // 0 from the pool is "unknown", not "empty": no pass on a guess.
+    if (IdleTexturePressureEnabled() && eden_pool_largest_free) {
+        const auto now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+        if (now >= idle_pressure_next) {
+            idle_pressure_next = now + std::chrono::milliseconds(250);
+            const u64 largest_free = eden_pool_largest_free();
+            if (largest_free != 0 && largest_free < 1024_MiB) {
+                RefusalEvict(64_MiB, false, true);
+            }
+        }
+    }
+#endif
     if (MemoryCensus::Enabled()) {
         CensusTick();
     }
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
index 9b24c51..ae3a93e 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
@@ -533,7 +533,11 @@ public:
     /// images wait for TickFrame) is back for the retry. "Need no copy back" = !IsDownloadable,
     /// as in AreaEvict and the collector, so GPU-written images that cannot be copied back (MSAA
     /// without CanDownloadMsaa, TrimmedLevels, unbacked) go without a copy. Returns bytes deleted.
-    u64 RefusalEvict(u64 wanted, bool in_join);
+    /// `idle` (EDEN_NX2_IDLE_TEXTURE_PRESSURE, never with `in_join`): no refusal yet, so only
+    /// images unused for 1 s and never written by the GPU.
+    u64 RefusalEvict(u64 wanted, bool in_join, bool idle = false);
+    /// EDEN_NX2_IDLE_TEXTURE_PRESSURE: when the pool is looked at next (TickFrame).
+    std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point idle_pressure_next{};
 
     /// EDEN_NX2_REFUSAL_EVICT=1, at the end of a frame after RefusalEvict passed GPU-written
     /// images over: copies back and deletes up to 8 of them, each up to 32 MiB and 64 MiB in all,
